# How to cite this tool and its dataset. See https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this tool or its dataset, please cite it as below, with the version or commit you
  used. The timing bound has not been validated against hardware (N = 0); say so if you rely on it.
title: "mcu-ruleout: best-case rule-outs for C kernels on Cortex-M0+ and Cortex-M4F microcontrollers"
type: software
authors:
  # As the name appears in LICENSE. Replace with given-names and family-names if you prefer.
  - name: "DavidDruker"
version: 0.2.0.dev0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DavidDruker/MCUMatch"
abstract: >-
  A command-line tool that says when a C kernel cannot fit or cannot meet a deadline on a
  Cortex-M0+ or Cortex-M4F microcontroller, even in the best case. It compares a lower bound on
  what the code needs (the smallest build, and the documented minimum cycle count of every executed
  instruction) with an upper bound on what the part offers (cited capacities and the maximum rated
  clock). It never says that code fits. The repository also holds a dataset of published timing
  measurements with their configurations, and a pre-registered validation.
keywords:
  - cortex-m
  - embedded
  - microcontroller
  - lower bound
  - execution time
  - static analysis
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "Published timing measurements of DSP and control kernels on Cortex-M0+ and Cortex-M4F"
    authors:
      - name: "DavidDruker"
    license: CC-BY-4.0
    notes: "data/published_measurements.csv and data/sources.csv in this repository. Each source keeps its own terms."
